.TH QUADRF-LORA-PHY 1 "August 2026" "quadrf-mesh 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quadrf-lora-phy \- experimental QuadRF LoRa-compatible PHY and Air-IPC daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-lora-phy
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadrf-lora-phy
owns the QuadRF radio, modulates and demodulates air frames, and serves
Air-IPC version 1 on a local Unix socket. Invoked without a mode flag it
uses FPGA digital loopback. The packaged systemd unit defaults to
.BR --ota .
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B quadrf-lora-phy --help
for the complete option list. The production socket default is
.IR /run/quadrf/phy.sock .
.SH FILES
.I /etc/default/quadrf-lora-phy
contains service defaults.
.SH WARNING
The operator is responsible for lawful RF configuration and operation.
.SH AUTHOR
Roy C. Gross.
